.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-restore 1  "restore " 
.SH NAME
murk\-restore \- Print the key encoded by a BIP39 recovery phrase (saves nothing)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk restore\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the key encoded by a BIP39 recovery phrase (saves nothing)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename, for the restored\-identity recipient check
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
